Permitted Use

Sliqtly may be used free of charge for:

1. Personal Use

   Use by an individual for personal, educational, hobby, or other
   non-commercial purposes.

2. Solo Business Use

   Commercial use by a business is permitted free of charge only if all of
   the following conditions are met:

   * the business is operated by a single individual;
   * the business has no employees, excluding independent contractors
     engaged on an occasional basis;
   * the business is not owned, controlled by, or operated on behalf of
     another company or organization; and
   * the business has annual gross revenue of less than EUR 200,000 during
     its most recently completed financial year.

   For newly established businesses without a completed financial year, the
   EUR 200,000 threshold applies to reasonably expected annual gross revenue.

Any commercial use outside these conditions requires a separate commercial
license from the copyright holder.

Examples of Use Requiring a Commercial License

A commercial license is required for use by, or primarily for the benefit
of:

* companies with more than one employee;
* companies with annual gross revenue of EUR 200,000 or more;
* teams or departments within a larger organization;
* corporations, partnerships, agencies, consultancies, institutions, or
  other organizations that do not qualify for Solo Business Use;
* a subsidiary, affiliate, or contractor using Sliqtly primarily for the
  benefit of an organization that would otherwise require a commercial
  license.

No Transfer of Eligibility

A qualifying individual or Solo Business may not use its license to provide
Sliqtly as an internal tool, hosted service, or shared installation for
another organization that would otherwise require a commercial license.

